I'll think of, like, a line.
-Okay.

00:08:51.463 --> 00:08:53.298
-Like you could put in, like,
a haiku or some [bleep].

00:08:53.298 --> 00:08:56.235
And I'll be like, okay,
this will be the song,

00:08:56.235 --> 00:08:57.536
and this is where it comes from.

00:08:57.536 --> 00:08:58.971
And sometimes that looks like

00:08:58.971 --> 00:09:02.008
rewriting the song
like a billion times,

00:09:02.008 --> 00:09:03.742
because sometimes
I do get too specific

00:09:03.742 --> 00:09:05.211
and people are like,
you're going to --

00:09:05.211 --> 00:09:06.378
-Yeah.

00:09:06.378 --> 00:09:07.813
-You're going to get
in trouble legally.

00:09:07.813 --> 00:09:10.182
You're going to have problems.
I'm like, "I don't care."

00:09:10.182 --> 00:09:12.184
And I do, I do care.
I care --

00:09:12.184 --> 00:09:13.185
I care quite a bit.

00:09:13.185 --> 00:09:14.453
[ Laughter ]

00:09:14.453 --> 00:09:16.788
But yeah, so it looks
different all the time.

00:09:16.788 --> 00:09:18.791
But I love writing.
-And do you --

00:09:18.791 --> 00:09:20.692
Do you get --
How do you get excited?

00:09:20.692 --> 00:09:22.194
When you realize you have
a song that you love...

00:09:22.194 --> 00:09:23.262
-Yeah.

00:09:23.262 --> 00:09:24.263
-Do you get excited
in the process?

00:09:24.263 --> 00:09:25.597
Do you --
Does your sort of

00:09:25.597 --> 00:09:26.932
does your pulse start to race
when you're like,

00:09:26.932 --> 00:09:28.300
oh, I think we got a hold
of a good one here.

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:29.401
-Oh, I get --
I get so excited.

00:09:29.401 --> 00:09:30.836
Sometimes
I'm so excited that I cry

00:09:30.836 --> 00:09:34.173
because I'm very, like,
I react, like, to music.

00:09:34.173 --> 00:09:35.907
I think a lot of people do,
but like for me

00:09:35.907 --> 00:09:37.710
it's always been very physical.

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:38.911
Like, I, like,
have little, like,

00:09:38.911 --> 00:09:40.946
twitches and, like, tics
and things like that.

00:09:40.946 --> 00:09:43.949
And I used to feel,
like, very weird about it.

00:09:43.949 --> 00:09:45.383
And now that I work
with, like, pretty much

00:09:45.383 --> 00:09:46.919
the same people
all the time,

00:09:46.919 --> 00:09:49.488
and I work with, like, a lot of
people who are my best friends,

00:09:49.488 --> 00:09:51.623
they, like, see me, like,
tic and like twitch

00:09:51.623 --> 00:09:53.392
and, like, start to cry
and, like, hyperventilate.

00:09:53.392 --> 00:09:54.894
And they're like,
"Yeah."

00:09:54.894 --> 00:09:56.128
[ Laughter ]

00:09:56.128 --> 00:09:58.230
-Well,
I'm so happy you're here.

00:09:58.230 --> 00:09:59.532
It's such a delight
to meet you.

00:09:59.532 --> 00:10:00.532
And I'm so thrilled you're
sticking around

00:10:00.532 --> 00:10:01.534
and do a song for us.

00:10:01.534 --> 00:10:02.635
-Thanks.
Thanks for having me.

00:10:02.635 --> 00:10:03.802
-Alright, you guys,
that's Reneé Rapp.

00:10:03.802 --> 00:10:04.903
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:04.903 --> 00:10:06.838
Her album "Snow Angels'
is available now.

00:10:06.838 --> 00:10:08.440
Stick around,
we'll be right back

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:10.576
with a performance
from Reneé Rapp.

